      children: "HtmlMesh instances by default are \\"in scene\\" meaning that they can be occluded by objects in scene and may occlude objects in scene when they are between the camera and the object. In scene HtmlMesh instances require that the scene clear color is transparent, and they must be rectangular. HttmlMesh instances can also be created as \\"overlays\\". In this case, they render in front of the scene, can be semi-transparent, and can be non-rectangular. However, overlays will render in front of all scene content, even content that is between the mesh and the camera. Overlays are a good choice when you want an HTML overlay to be attached to an object in the scene, as it eliminates the need to handle the projection and transforming of the HTML element yourself."
